  "worked_solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}\u2061A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\u2220A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{\u00a0cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m\u2220A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}} & =\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m\u2220A & ={45}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
